              ¦pS!                                                
              `--------- Brings You Today : DoorLister v1.0 beta


Simply this door displays an list of all your available doors, and the
commands to run them.

## INSTALLATION #############################################################

Getting the door to run:
Simply run this door as an normal amiexpress door, as methods of running doors
vary between different versions of amiexpress that part was chosen not to be 
included. Just refer to your amiexpress documentation. The door is written 
in c++ and has been tested on amiexpress versions 2.34,2.39,3.9,3.20 and 
3.32 so there shouldn`t be any problem getting it to run. 

The config file:
There should be a config file named 'doors.data' that should be located
in your s:. There`s a sample of the config file included in the pack,
but just to make sure you`ll get the hang of it i`ll explain it in the 
doc to.

It could look something like this:
*Sent                            ## The command to get it to run
@Edit Your Private Sent-By Line  ## The description of the door!

And you can have as many doors as you want in the file, just dont forget
to place the config file in s:  (s:doors.data)

## FILES INCLUDED IN THE ARCHIVE ############################################

name						original filesize			description
--------------------------------------------------------
doorsv11.exe    		13180							The compiled file to run
doorsv11.doc			2162							The documentation
doors.data				224							The config file

